§ `8. Article 40(1): which suspected breaches open an investigation`

`may investigate` MEANS `Article 40(1) and (2): the Minister may require me to submit materials, or have officials investigate, including entering my offices to inspect records and things`
`may not investigate` MEANS `Article 40(1) does not list this provision: a suspected breach of it does not trigger the Article 40 fact-finding power`

#ASSERT `Article 40(1): may the Minister investigate a suspected breach of` `Article 31(1), prior notice to users` EQUALS `may not investigate`
#ASSERT `Article 40(1): may the Minister investigate a suspected breach of` `Article 31(2), marking generative AI output` EQUALS `may investigate`
#ASSERT `Article 40(1): may the Minister investigate a suspected breach of` `Article 31(3), notice or marking of realistic synthetic output` EQUALS `may investigate`
#ASSERT `Article 40(1): may the Minister investigate a suspected breach of` `Article 32(1), the safety measures` EQUALS `may investigate`
#ASSERT `Article 40(1): may the Minister investigate a suspected breach of` `Article 32(2), submitting the results to the Minister` EQUALS `may investigate`
#ASSERT `Article 40(1): may the Minister investigate a suspected breach of` `Article 33(1), reviewing whether AI is high-impact` EQUALS `may not investigate`
#ASSERT `Article 40(1): may the Minister investigate a suspected breach of` `Article 34(1), measures for high-impact AI` EQUALS `may investigate`
#ASSERT `Article 40(1): may the Minister investigate a suspected breach of` `Article 36(1), designating a domestic representative` EQUALS `may not investigate`

